A `--set` override reaches the migrations gate and wins over the tiers: the project tier turns
`core.auto_migrate` off, but `--set core.auto_migrate=TRUE` — a string, read as a YAML-ish
boolean — turns the gate back into the auto-migrate order.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
-- fixtures/home/Claude/probe/config.yaml --
core:
  auto_migrate: false
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-gated/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-gated
title: Gated
summary: Must not render while the vault is behind.
---

Preamble that a working gate suppresses.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-gated/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  only: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-gated/only/prompt.md --
---
name: only
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-gated --set core.auto_migrate=TRUE
